    "fileId": 25372,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "IgG4-related sialadenitis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "IgG4-related submandibular gland disease with extensive fibrosis and glandular atrophy. Uninvolved parenchyma is present in the left upper field.",
    "source": "Wah Cheuk",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/25372.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/thumb_25372.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57076,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 236,
    "fileId": 25373,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "IgG4-related sialadenitis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "There is a variable lymphoid infiltrate in the parenchyma, and the lobular architecture of the salivary gland is accentuated by septal fibrosis.",
    "source": "Wah Cheuk",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/25373.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/thumb_25373.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57077,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 236,
    "fileId": 25374,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "IgG4-related sialadenitis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The lymphoid infiltrate comprises plasma cells and small lymphocytes with some reactive lymphoid follicles.",
    "source": "Wah Cheuk",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/25374.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/thumb_25374.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57078,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 236,
    "fileId": 25375,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "IgG4-related sialadenitis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "There is preferential loss of acini and some of the residual ductal structures show periductal fibrosis.",
    "source": "Wah Cheuk",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/25375.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/thumb_25375.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 57079,
    "bookid": 52,
    "chapterId": 236,
    "fileId": 25376,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "IgG4-related sialadenitis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "The lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate typically does not involve the glandular epithelium, i.e. there are no lymphoepithelial lesions.",
    "source": "Wah Cheuk",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/25376.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/52/236/thumb_25376.jpg"
  },
