    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\">Common sites involved by IgG4-related disease and the salient clinical features</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Wah Cheuk",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 697.4pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"930\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Affected site(s)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Nomenclature (related/obsolete&nbsp;terminology)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4+ cell <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">count<sup>a</sup></span></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Salient clinical <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">features</span></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Pancreas</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related pancreatitis (autoimmune pancreatitis type&nbsp;I; lymphoplasmacytic pancreatitis)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2 </sup>(biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Parenchymal mass lesion mimicking pancreatic carcinoma (painless obstructive jaundice, pancreatic mass, abdominal pain) and/or pancreatic insufficiency (new-onset diabetes mellitus, steatorrhoea)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Sausage-shaped pancreas with delayed enhancement, capsule-like low-density rim, main pancreatic duct narrowing without upstream dilatation on contrast CT/MRI </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{32297064}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Hepatobiliary system</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related sclerosing cholangitis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Biliary obstruction mimicking cholangiocarcinoma (obstructive jaundice, abnormal liver function tests) or primary sclerosing cholangitis but exhibiting dramatic response to steroids; frequently associated with IgG4-related pancreatitis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Diffuse or segmental narrowing of bile ducts and wall thickening on cholangiogram </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{30575336}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IgG4-related cholecystitis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mass lesion mimicking cancer (right upper quadrant pain, jaundice) <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{24944152}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related hepatic inflammatory pseudotumour</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Probably represents intrahepatic involvement of IgG4-related sclerosing cholangitis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Hepatic mass and abnormal liver function tests; contrast-enhancing mass lesion with dilatation of intrahepatic and peripheral bile ducts </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{31358425}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Orbit, including lacrimal glands</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related ophthalmic disease, IgG4-related orbital inflammation, IgG4-related orbital myositis (orbital pseudotumour, idiopathic fibroinflammatory disease, idiopathic orbital inflammation)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;400/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Unilateral or bilateral painless orbital swelling, proptosis, and diplopia; rarely eye pain and visual impairment</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Contrast-enhancing soft tissue mass; preferentially affecting lateral rectus muscle, in contrast to Graves ophthalmopathy; bilateral infraorbital nerve involvement on imaging is pathognomonic of IgG4-related ophthalmic disease </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{33068267; 33402162; 17414116}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Salivary glands</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related sialadenitis (K&uuml;ttner tumour, chronic sclerosing sialadenitis)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;400/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Unilateral or bilateral painless swelling most commonly involving submandibular gland; occasionally simultaneous bilateral lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular gland involvement (Mikulicz disease); xerostomia is usually mild and responds well to steroids, in contrast to Sj&ouml;gren syndrome; sialography normal </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{26194097}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Retroperitoneum, mediastinum, and aorta</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related retroperitoneal fibrosis (Ormond disease)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;120/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Asymptomatic or nonspecific constitutional symptoms (fatigue, anorexia, fever, weight loss), low back or flank pain, leg oedema, abnormal renal function test</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Imaging shows soft tissue mass over paravertebral area and pelvis, frequently involving abdominal aorta and iliac arteries (IgG4-related periaortitis) and entrapping ureter, causing hydronephrosis </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{31942203; 30754935}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IgG4-related mediastinal fibrosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;120/mm<sup>2</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Thoracic counterpart of retroperitoneal fibrosis and often manifests simultaneously; frequently involves thoracic aorta (IgG4-related aortitis/periaortitis)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Asymptomatic or dyspnoea, haemoptysis, dysphagia, and chest pain <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{29851832}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 14; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related aortitis/periaortitis/periarteritis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Most commonly involves infrarenal abdominal aorta and iliac arteries in the context of retroperitoneal fibrosis or thoracic aorta, less commonly other medium-sized arteries (coronary and mesenteric arteries); asymptomatic or low back pain, some may present with aortic aneurysm or dissection</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Imaging shows vessel wall thickening (media and adventitia), mass-like lesion with contrast enhancement with or without luminal dilatation (aneurysm) or reduction; PET-CT useful to assess disease activity and detect asymptomatic lesions </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{33121641; 31942203}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 15; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymph node</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 16; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related lymphadenopathy</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;400/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Incidental lymphadenopathy on imaging, painless non-tender lymph nodes, often adjacent to organs affected by IgG4-related disease, local mass effects (hydronephrosis, lower limb swelling for pelvic lymph nodes)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Lymph nodes usually mildly enlarged (mean: 20&nbsp;mm) with homogeneous enhancement and no calcification or necrosis </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{18344866; 30558692}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 17; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Kidney</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 18; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related renal disease</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;120/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Incidental finding on imaging or abnormal renal function tests/urinalysis, hypocomplementaemia or elevated serum IgE is common</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Contrast CT shows multiple low-density lesions, diffuse kidney enlargement, hypovascular solitary masses </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{33398598}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 19; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Dura and pituitary</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 20; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IgG4-related pachymeningitis (idiopathic hypertrophic pachymeningitis)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Headache, cranial nerve palsies, visual impairment, motor weakness, numbness, seizures, cognitive decline, and gait instability </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{29061247; 24384648}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 21; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IgG4-related hypophysitis (lymphocytic hypophysitis)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Headache, visual field defect, hyperprolactinaemia (galactorrhoea), hypopituitarism (diabetes insipidus, fatigue, amenorrhoea) <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{31929792; 21593109}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 22; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Skin and soft tissue</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 23; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IgG4-related skin disease (cutaneous pseudolymphoma)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IgG4-related soft tissue disease (idiopathic cervical fibrosis; cutaneous pseudolymphoma)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;800/mm<sup>2 </sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Plaques or indurated nodules frequently in the head and neck region, local neurological symptoms (numbness and shoulder drop) due to associated nerve involvement is common <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{20871392}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 24; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Lung and pleura</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 25; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IgG4-related lung disease, IgG4-related pleuritis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;80/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Incidental finding of abnormal chest imaging, or cough, chest pain, dyspnoea, haemoptysis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nodules, ground-glass opacities, bronchial wall&nbsp;/ bronchovascular bundle thickening, interlobular septal wall thickening, infiltrative shadow, pleural thickening or effusion <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{26879484; 31227290}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 26; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 262.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"350\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Thyroid</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 27; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 2.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"76\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 205.55pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"274\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IgG4-related thyroiditis (Riedel thyroiditis; fibrosing Hashimoto thyroiditis)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.5pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;80/mm<sup>2</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 314.65pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"420\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">At least some of Riedel thyroiditis and fibrosing variant of Hashimoto thyroiditis represent IgG4-related disease; presents with goitre and/or hypothyroidism <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{33311000}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">a</span></sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">IgG4</span>-related disease cannot be diagnosed solely on the basis of IgG4-positive plasma cell count.</p>",
